Let $D$ be the determinant of the matrix
\[
A = \begin{pmatrix}
\sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\
\cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\
1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x
\end{pmatrix}.
\]
We want to find the possible values of $D$ as $x$ ranges over all real numbers.
We can expand the determinant as follows:
\begin{align*} D &= \sec^2 x \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} - 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} + 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) + (\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} \cos^2 x) - \cos^2 x \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \sec^2 x \left( \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} \right) - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\sec^2 x \cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\sec^2 x \cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\frac{1}{\cos^2 x} \cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\frac{1}{\cos^2 x} \cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x - \cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x (1 - \cos^2 x)}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x = \frac{\cos^2 x \sin^2 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cos^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x = \cos^4 x. \end{align*}
Thus $D = \cos^4 x$. Since $x$ ranges over all real numbers, $\cos x$ can take any value between $-1$ and $1$. Therefore $\cos^4 x$ can take any value in the interval $[0,1]$. 

We are asked to find the possible values of $D$, so we want the range of $\cos^4 x$. Since $-1 \le \cos x \le 1$, we have $0 \le \cos^2 x \le 1$, and $0 \le \cos^4 x \le 1$. 
Therefore the possible values of $D = \cos^4 x$ are in the interval $[0,1]$. 

