\begin{align*} 8888 \div 8 &= 1111 \text{ remainder } 0 \\ 1111 \div 8 &= 138 \text{ remainder } 7 \\ 138 \div 8 &= 17 \text{ remainder } 2 \\ 17 \div 8 &= 2 \text{ remainder } 1 \\ 2 \div 8 &= 0 \text{ remainder } 2 \end{align*} Reading the remainders in reverse order, we have $8888_{10} = 21270_8$.

Step 2: Find the sum of the digits of the base-8 expression $21270_8$. The digits are 2, 1, 2, 7, and 0. Their sum is $2+1+2+7+0 = 12$.

