Let the original cube have side length $s_1 = 2$ cm. The volume of the original cube is $V_1 = s_1^3 = 2^3 = 8$ cubic centimeters.

The volume is increased by 19 cubic centimeters, so the new volume $V_2$ is $V_2 = V_1 + 19 = 8 + 19 = 27$ cubic centimeters.

Let the side length of the new cube be $s_2$. Since the new cube has a volume of 27 cubic centimeters, we have $s_2^3 = 27$.
Taking the cube root of both sides, we get $s_2 = \sqrt[3]{27} = 3$ cm.

The length of the edge of the new cube is 3 cm.

