The volume of a 2-cm-by-2-cm-by-2-cm cube is $2^3 = 8$ cubic centimeters. 
This volume is increased by 19 cubic centimeters to form a larger cube. So the larger cube has a volume of $8 + 19 = 27$ cubic centimeters. 
Let $s$ be the length of the edge of the larger cube. Then $s^3 = 27$, so $s = \sqrt[3]{27} = 3$. 
The length of the edge of the new cube is 3 cm.

